  "observed": [
    "Upgrade retains all seven legacy audit identities and every old logical field; new policy_revision NULL. NULL config or policy rejected23514, individually valid but mixed revisions rejected23503.",
    "Actual PostgreSQL DDL rewrites audit heap: relfilenode17195\u219217734 and xmin751\u2192752, with identical logical rows. Applied807 checksum unchanged; ordinary retry/rollback xmins still compared.",
    "One immutable issue receipt binds each successful session to its actual principal, session ID and validated config/policy. No session token/hash/password/peer/raw username is copied to audit.",
    "Explicit logout appends once. Repeated logout after a new Control incarnation leaves complete session/audit rows and xmin unchanged. Legacy/reset revocation receives no invented logout attribution.",
    "Injected audit INSERT refusal returns Backend and rolls back issuance plus terminal cleanup, or logout. New Control performs successful explicit retry. Unchanged retry preserves original audit.",
    "Startup refuses missing807 with all other privileges present, and refuses missing audit INSERT independently. Existing missing806/DELETE, Origin/CSRF, policy drift and late-client scenarios also pass.",
    "Actual session COMMIT pass/before-forward/after-complete yields issue audit counts1/1/2 and logout audit counts1/1/2, joined to exact session/principal/config/policy. Four unknown branches emit no HTTP bytes/cookies and exit4; same logout retry does not duplicate attribution.",
    "Target proxy requires exactly one target Execute completion and selected COMMIT despite the additional audit INSERT. Synthetic wire RED counted2; corrected proxy counts1. Early error-before-Execute/Sync regression also has executed RED/green.",
    "Four TCP clients completed4069 self requests in12011ms while policy renewed. SIGTERM with incomplete sockets took10ms in this run and left no Control clients. These are small-workload observations, not capacity or universal latency bounds."
  ],
